---
/**
 * Confidentialité : le site (aucun cookie, aucune mesure d'audience, journaux de l'hébergeur, téléchargements comptés
 * par GitHub), le compte TaskForce (obligatoire pour l'app desktop : nom, e-mail, mot de passe haché ; connexion,
 * rapatriement des projets web, e-mails sur le service), l'app desktop (données locales, aucune télémétrie, connexions
 * choisies), les droits RGPD. Le serveur de comptes est hébergé chez OVH, en France.
 */
import LegalDoc from "@/layouts/LegalDoc.astro";
import { LINKS } from "@/lib/site";
---

<LegalDoc
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="The TaskForce website uses no cookies and no analytics. The desktop app keeps your projects on your computer: your free TaskForce account is the only thing we hold."
  updated="20 October 2026"
>
  <h2>In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and runs <strong>no analytics</strong> or advertising trackers.</li>
    <li>
      The desktop app needs a <strong>free TaskForce account</strong>. We keep your account; your projects stay on your
      computer, and the app sends us no usage data.
    </li>
    <li>The services you connect to the app receive data directly from your computer, under their own terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    Pierre Michel, the publisher of TaskForce (see the <a href="/legal/notice">legal notice</a>), is responsible for
    the processing described here. For any question about your data, write to{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> Vercel, our host, processes technical data such as your IP address and browser
      details to serve the pages and protect the site from abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts and images</strong> are served by this site itself: no request goes to a third party while you
      read.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Downloads</strong> are served by GitHub from the project's releases, under GitHub's privacy statement.
      GitHub counts how many times each file is downloaded: we only see those totals, never who downloaded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email.</strong> If you write to us, we use your address and your message only to answer you, and we
      delete them once they are no longer needed.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your TaskForce account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What we keep.</strong> Your email address, your name, and your password, which our sign-in service only
      stores as a secure hash. The account you used on the web app is the same account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why.</strong> To sign you in to the app; to copy your work between the web app and your computer, when
      you ask; and to email you about TaskForce itself, such as updates, changes to these terms or the closing of the
      web app. We send no advertising.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Where.</strong> On our account server, hosted by OVH SAS in France.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal basis.</strong> Providing the account you asked for, and our legitimate interest in telling you
      about changes to the service.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Emails</strong> are sent through Brevo, our email provider.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long.</strong> As long as your account exists. Ask us to delete it at any time, and we delete it with
      everything attached to it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The desktop app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your data stays on your computer.</strong> Projects, notes, attachments and settings are kept
      in the app's data folder. We have no access to them, unless you copy a workspace or a project to the web app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Signing in.</strong> The app talks to our account server to sign you in and, when you ask, to copy your
      work between the web app and your computer. It sends nothing else, and after the first sign-in it also works
      offline.
    </li>
    <li><strong>No telemetry.</strong> The app sends no usage data, to us or to anyone else.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connections you choose.</strong> When you add an AI provider's API key, start Claude Code, or connect
      GitHub, Copilot, MCP servers, Plane or webhooks, the data they need goes from your computer straight to that
      service, under its own terms and privacy policy. We are never in between.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Updates.</strong> The app asks GitHub whether a new version exists, so GitHub receives that request.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The web app</h2>
  <p>
    Until it closes, the hosted web app at app.taskforce-project.fr is covered by its own privacy policy, shown in the
    app. Its projects are deleted when it closes; your account stays. To take your projects with you, see{" "}
    <a href="/migrate">moving from the web app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can access, correct, delete or export the personal data we hold about you, including your
    account, and object to or restrict its processing. Write to <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.email}`}>{LINKS.email}</a>.
    You can also lodge a complaint with your data protection authority: in France, the CNIL (cnil.fr).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we update it on this page, change the date above, and tell account holders by email.</p>
</LegalDoc>
